Package: gaffke
Type: Package
Title: The Gaffke Confidence Interval for the Mean of a Discrete Bounded Variable
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Louis", "Abraham", email = "abraham.cie@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes the Gaffke confidence interval for the mean of a
    variable that takes a finite set of known values, from the counts of
    each value. The interval generalizes the Clopper-Pearson interval, and
    its coverage is at least the nominal level for every sample size and
    every distribution (Gaffke (2005), Mathematical Methods of Statistics 14(4);
    Vlassis and Thomas (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2607.08415>). The
    endpoints are quantiles of a weighted sum of Dirichlet variables,
    computed by a Fourier inversion integral on a line through the saddle
    point, with a small relative error also far in the tails; the package
    also gives the distribution function, density and quantile function of
    this law.
